# Architecture Pressure LLM Guide

## Purpose

Use this command to find callable and public API pressure points in the configured architecture root.

## When To Run

- Before simplifying a feature module.
- Before changing public module seams or re-export files.
- When a workflow feels like it is forwarding too many values through too many functions.

## How To Read The Result

- Most Calling highlights callables with the highest direct fan-out.
- Most Called highlights resolved internal call targets with the most callers.
- Wide Signatures highlights callables most likely to carry prop-drilled values.
- Re-export Hubs highlights files that forward symbols from implementation modules.
- Public API Hubs highlights broad package seams, even when modwire does not classify them as re-exports.

## Agent Tips

- Confirm high-pressure targets by reading the code before refactoring.
- Prefer removing unused public exports before introducing new abstraction.
- Do not treat unresolved calls as proof; use them as a signal that static resolution needs human review.
- Pair this with `architecture shape` after changing imports, signatures, or package seams.
